I have an AlphaStation 200 4/233 and I want to install DEC Unix 4.0.
I've read the install documentation on the 'net and found references to
the SCSI disk drives (RZ's) that are recommended.  I however, want to
use a standard SCSI drive.  Is this possible?  I also found in the
install docs the partition table setup for each of the recommended RZ
drives.   Will I have to replicate this partitioning on my OTS drive?
There are overlaid partitions on the RZs.  How do I do this?  Is there a
disk partitioning tool available from the SRM?   Can I use the SRM to
wipe out the partition tables on the new drive.   I've installed other
Unix's and they all have some tool for patitioning the disk as the OS
needs it.  Is this available in the DU install?

  TIA,

    Nathan Rosales



