I'm using an IBM 9G 39100W UltraWide hard disk in my Personal Workstation
600au.  I've also installed an IBM 4G 34330W drive in an ancient 
DEC 3000/300 using a 68-pin to 50-pin SCSI adapter.

I had no trouble getting either drive to work using the Digital UNIX
disk management tool, though I've only attempted to set up fixed
partitions, not ones that I could grow.

I think you should be able to get almost any SCSI hard disk to work
with your 200 4/233:  your only worry is PHYSICALLY getting the disk
in there!  You might have trouble fitting things in.

